WEBVTT

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:05.590
This Resolve button closes a support ticket.
Where is the callback defined?

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.190
And how does it reach the button?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:12.790
Trace in source follows a prop through your
code, even when a component gives it a new
name.

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:16.310
With Queue selected and a matching source
analysis loaded,

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:18.310
choose onResolve in Props.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.910
Under Supplied by, the callback starts in
DeskApp.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:25.190
Queue passes it to TicketRow as onDismiss.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.670
Follow the link to a mounted ticket row.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.030
Its click handler calls onDismiss with the
ticket ID.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.310
Try it on the page. Click Resolve on that
row.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.630
The ticket changes to resolved.
